@prefix : <https://w3id.org/fdso/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/fdso/> .

<https://w3id.org/fdso/> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                          owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/fdso/1.0> ;
                          <http://omv.ontoware.org/2005/05/ontology#designedForOntologyTask> """1)To act as a data model which incorporates the agents that are reponsible for supporting the various reposne task in case of flood scenario.
2)To act as a data model which incorporates the resources in terms of rescue equipments,  relief materials and required data to carry out reposne task."""@en ;
                          <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "Flood Disaster Support Ontology (FDSO) provides an ontological data model to support urban flood disaster response. It can be used as a data model that can accommodate the various organizations and agents of different levels of the administrative agencies that are part of the flood disaster management process. It depicts their relationships and their activities specifically during an urban flood disaster response. The ontology also organizes the resources and the information about them that are possessed by different organizations and may be used by first responders to carry out the activities like rescue and relief."@en ;
                          <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/issued> "2022-06-27" ;
                          <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/modified> "2023-02-18" ;
                          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Biswanath Dutta"@en ,
                                                             "Prashant Kumar Sinha"@en ;
                          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Flood Disaster Support Ontology"@en ;
                          <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "fdso"@en ;
                          <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceURI> "http://www.isibang.ac.in/ns/fdso" ;
                          <http://www.isibang.ac.in/ns/mod#browsingUI> "http://www.isibang.ac.in/ns/fdso"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                          rdfs:comment "" ;
                          <https://w3id.org/mod#competencyQuestions> """CQ1) What were the causes of the flood that occurred? What area was affected due to the flood and to which taluk of Bengaluru does the area belong? What time does the flood start? Who were the nodal agents that were responsible for the flood situation? What objects were affected by the flood situation?
CQ2) What type of flood forecasting agent is the central water commission? Which agent is supervising the central water commission? Who is the head of the central water commission? What kinds of data are available with the central water commission? To which agent the central water commission passes the information?
CQ3) Who establishes Bengaluru Emergency Operation Centre? What are the contact details of the Bengaluru Emergency Operation Centre and which agents are coordinating with it?
CQ4) Who performs the boat lifting victim task? What are the data and resources required for such a task?
CQ5) What type of resource is a life jacket? Who has the resource life jackets? What is the resource code? What specific quantities it’s available? Who are the contact people for the resource?
CQ6) What were the activities that were carried out for the response process to the flood?
CQ7) What are the different flood forecasting agents?
CQ8) Which state ministries have a representative nodal officer for an emergency situation?
CQ9) What are the tasks performed by KSNDMC? Which organization supervises it? What kind of data is available with them and who needs to be contacted? To which organization the data is passed during a flood situation?  
CQ10) List out all the resources in ascending order along with the quantities available with the organization. Also, list out the person and contact details for the resource."""@en .

