###  https://w3id.org/fdso/#GeospatialDepartments
<https://w3id.org/fdso/#GeospatialDepartments> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/fdso/#CentralLineDepartments> ,
                                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                 owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/fdso/#passesInformationTo> ;
                                                                 owl:someValuesFrom <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent>
                                                               ] ;
                                               rdfs:comment "Geospatial department consists of information that characterizes objects, events or alternative elements with a position on or near the surface of the earth. Geospatial depatment typically combines position knowledge (generally co-ordinates on the earth) and associate knowledge (the qualities of the object, event or phenomena involved) with temporal knowledge (the time or life span at which the position and attributes happen). The location provided may be static in the short term (for example, the location of a piece of equipment, an earthquake event, children living in poverty) or dynamic (for example, a moving vehicle or pedestrian, the spread of an infectious disease)."@en ;
                                               rdfs:label "GeospatialDepartments"@en .


